cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this audit or the derived analysis set, please cite this repository
  together with Severson et al. (2019) and the underlying dataset, both listed
  under `references`.
title: >-
  A data-quality audit of the MIT-Stanford-TRI fast-charging battery dataset,
  with a reproducible analysis set
abstract: >-
  An independent, read-only audit of the Severson/Attia fast-charging battery
  dataset (124 published A123 APR18650M1A LFP/graphite cells in three batches),
  read directly from the raw MATLAB v7.3 files rather than from the pre-built
  pickles. The audit recovers the barcode and channel_id fields that the upstream
  documentation reports as unavailable, resolves the 140 struct rows to 135
  physical cells, tests all 21 claims made on the four dataset documentation
  pages, records twelve substantive problems that no page mentions, and publishes
  a documented analysis set of 135 cells and 113,559 cycles with per-cycle quality
  flags. No cycle is masked, imputed or smoothed.
type: software
authors:
